`neutron dev` runs the SDK's dev server (`python -m neutron dev app.main:app`)
with auto-reload, using `.venv/bin/python` when it exists.

The SDK (`{{.SDK.Name}}`) is installed from the Neutron repository
(`{{.SDK.Source}}`, subdirectory `{{.SDK.Subdir}}`); it is not published on
PyPI, where `neutron` is an unrelated package.

## Endpoints

- `GET /api/hello` — sample route in `app/main.py`
- `GET /health` — built in: `{"status", "nucleus", "version"}`
- `GET /openapi.json`, `GET /docs` — built in

## Configuration

Read from the environment (`.env` lists them; nothing loads it automatically):

| Variable | Default |
|---|---|
| `NEUTRON_HOST` | `127.0.0.1` under `neutron dev`, else `0.0.0.0` |
| `NEUTRON_PORT` | `8000` |
| `NEUTRON_DATABASE_URL` | unset — `/health` reports `"nucleus": "unconfigured"` until you connect one |
| `NEUTRON_LOG_LEVEL` | `info` |
